  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For a given integer array AAA of length NNN, and satisfying 0≤Ai&lt;N0 \\le A_i &lt; N0≤Ai​&lt;N, and another integer parameter MMM (1≤M≤N1 \\le M \\le N1≤M≤N), define f(A,M)f(A, M)f(A,M) in the following way:\n\n\nStart with an empty set S={}S = \\{\\}S={}.\nFor each MMM length subsequence of AAA, i.e. all sequences of the form [Ai1,Ai2,…,AiM][A_{i_1}, A_{i_2}, \\ldots, A_{i_M}][Ai1​​,Ai2​​,…,AiM​​] with 1≤i1&lt;i2&lt;…&lt;iM≤N1 \\le i_1 &lt; i_2 &lt; \\ldots &lt; i_M \\le N1≤i1​&lt;i2​&lt;…&lt;iM​≤N, insert the MEX†^{\\dagger}† of the subsequence into SSS.\nf(A,M)f(A, M)f(A,M) is defined as the final size of the set SSS.\nLess formally, f(A,M)f(A, M)f(A,M) is the number of possible MEX-values from MMM-length subsequences of AAA.\n\nFor example, for A=[0,1,2]A = [0, 1, 2]A=[0,1,2] and M=2M = 2M=2, we will consider the subsequences [0,1],[0,2][0, 1], [0, 2][0,1],[0,2] and [1,2][1, 2][1,2], and the corresponding MEX values 222, 111 and 000. Thus, S={0,1,2}S = \\{0, 1, 2\\}S={0,1,2} and f(A,M)=3f(A, M) = 3f(A,M)=3.\n\nYou are given an integer NNN. For each integer MMM from 111 to NNN:\n\n\nfind the sum of f(A,M)f(A, M)f(A,M) over all **non-decreasing** arrays AAA satisfying the following conditions:\n\nA1≤A2≤…ANA_1 \\le A_2 \\le \\ldots A_NA1​≤A2​≤…AN​ (the non-decreasing condition)\n0≤Ai&lt;N0 \\le A_i &lt; N0≤Ai​&lt;N\n\n\nSince the answers can be large, output all of them modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of input for each test case contains a single integer NNN.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the answers for M=1,2,…,NM = 1, 2, \\ldots, NM=1,2,…,N modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105"
    ],
